"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=142810262", "extmetadata": {"DateTime": {"value": "2023-12-24 04:20:07", "source": "mediawiki-metadata", "hidden": ""}, "ObjectName": {"value": "Kalpeshwar Uttarakhand", "source": "mediawiki-metadata"}, "CommonsMetadataExtension": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "CC-Zero|Self-published work|Kalpeshwar Temple, Uttarakhand", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "Kalpeshwar is a village enroute to the fifth stop of Panch Kedar pilgrimage route in Uttarakhand.\n<p>The Kalpeshwar temple, also called Kalpnath temple, is a mountain side Shiva temple. It is the fifth stop of Panch Kedar (five Kedars) pilgrimage route. The sanctum, cave walls and the Shiva iconography here is also svayambhu-style (monolithic) in a manner similar to the Rudranath temple.\n</p>\nThe Kalpeshwar temple is accessible by another hiker's trail with waterfalls and wildflowers, past the scenic village of Kalpeshwar. It is only one of the five Kedar temples that remains open in winter.", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "2023-05-23", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "Ms Sarah Welch", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "LicenseShortName": {"value": "CC0", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "UsageTerms": {"value": "Creative Commons Zero, Public Domain Dedication", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "AttributionRequired": {"value": "false", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "LicenseUrl": {"value": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Copyrighted": {"value": "True", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "Restrictions": {"value": "", "source": "commons-desc-page",